From: Fenyx <ayushsoni2911@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(linux): use the native Xbox Bluetooth axis layout

The Xbox One/Series profiles identify as the Bluetooth controllers
(045e:0b20 / 045e:0b13) but advertised xpad-style usages: right stick on
Rx/Ry and triggers on Z/Rz. Consumers that pick the layout from the
vendor/product ID (Chromium's MapperXboxBluetooth, SDL mappings) expect
what the kernel produces for the real controller: right stick on
ABS_Z/ABS_RZ, left trigger on ABS_BRAKE, right trigger on ABS_GAS. With
the old usages Chromium showed RT as LT, LT as the right stick X, the
right stick Y as RT and the right stick X as the right stick Y.

Use the native usages (Z/Rz, Simulation Brake/Accelerator) in the UHID
descriptor and the same evdev codes on the uinput fallback. Byte layout
is unchanged, so HIDAPI consumers are unaffected.

Also tests Wine/Proton's XInput view (SDL3 HIDAPI descriptor parse + winebus).

Applied by Nova at configure time (cmake/compile_definitions/common.cmake).
---
